@startuml canonical-connective-owner-cursor
' ============================================================================
' Lifecycle of the canonical ConnectiveBody child cursor (task 10879).
'   BLUE  #1565C0  validation and the borrowed cursor
'   AMBER #EF6C00  the bind guard (pointer AND length) and its premise
'   GREEN #2E7D32  the owned cursor resuming over validated children
'   RED   #C62828  refusal: no counter is transferred
'   GREY  #616161  exhaustion
' Obligation numbers (1)-(4) refer to the Verus proof functions listed in
' canonical-connective-owner-refinement-2026-10-08.md.
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontSize 12
}

title <b>Canonical Connective child cursor</b>\nvalidate once, suspend by value, bind only the exact owner, resume

state "Borrowed" as Borrowed #BBDEFB
Borrowed : ""CanonicalConnectiveChildren(message, at, remaining)""
Borrowed : <latex>\mathrm{Valid}(b, c),\ \mathrm{Pos}(b, c, (0, n))</latex>
state "Suspended in a PDA frame" as Suspended #E3F2FD
Suspended : the cursor is ""Copy""; the frame keeps ""(at, remaining)""
Suspended : beside the pending child obligation
Suspended : <latex>\mathrm{Pos}(b, c, (a, r))</latex>
state Guard <<choice>>
state "Refused" as Refused #FFCDD2
Refused : ""Err(BodyMismatch)""
Refused : no owned cursor exists;
Refused : ""at"" and ""remaining"" were never copied
state "Owned" as Owned #C8E6C9
Owned : ""CanonicalOwnedConnectiveChildren(body, at, remaining)""
Owned : reads only ""body.as_ref()""
Owned : <latex>\mathrm{Pos}(b_o, c, (a, r)),\ b_o = b</latex>
state "Exhausted" as Exhausted #E0E0E0
Exhausted : ""next() = None""
Exhausted : <latex>r = 0,\ a = |b|</latex>

[*] -[#1565C0,thickness=2]-> Borrowed : ""new(message)"" validates every field-1 child:\nkey byte 10, minimal varint length, exact tiling
Borrowed -[#1565C0]-> Borrowed : borrowed ""next()"" while <latex>r > 0</latex>\nlends <latex>b[s_k, e_k)</latex>
Borrowed -[#1565C0]-> Suspended : PDA pushes the cursor\nbefore visiting a child
Suspended -[#EF6C00,thickness=2]-> Guard : ""bind_owned(owner)""\none ""as_ref()"" view
Guard -[#C62828,thickness=2]-> Refused : <latex>\alpha_o \neq \alpha_s \lor \ell_o \neq \ell_s</latex>\nobligation (1)
Guard -[#2E7D32,thickness=2]-> Owned : <latex>\alpha_o = \alpha_s \land \ell_o = \ell_s</latex>\ncounters moved unchanged, obligation (2)
Owned -[#2E7D32]-> Owned : ""next()"" while <latex>r > 0</latex>: returns <latex>[s_k, e_k)</latex>,\n<latex>(a, r) \leftarrow (e_k, r - 1)</latex>, obligation (3)
Owned -[#616161,thickness=2]-> Exhausted : ""next()"" when <latex>r = 0</latex>\nobligation (4)
Refused --> [*]
Exhausted --> [*]

note right of Guard #FFF3E0
  **Premise, not a proof:** the owner type implements the
  unsafe trait ""StableConnectiveBodyOwner"", so equal address
  and length imply equal bytes:
  <latex>\alpha_s = \alpha_o \land |b_s| = |b_o| \Rightarrow b_s = b_o</latex>
  Audited owners: ""&[u8]"", ""Vec<u8>"", ""ProtobufRegion"", ""EncodedRegion"".
  Length-only and pointer-only guards are the two bind mutants.
end note

note bottom of Owned #E8F5E9
  Exhaustion happens exactly after the validated suffix
  <latex>c_{n-r}, \ldots, c_{n-1}</latex> has been returned, in order.
  Skip-child, wrong-range and early-exhaustion are the three step mutants.
end note
@enduml
